<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-i-of-provence"><span class="enc-name">William I of Provence</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">William I of Provence, called the Liberator, was Count of Provence from about 968.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-i-of-sicily"><span class="enc-name">William I of Sicily</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">William I of Sicily, called the Bad, was King of Sicily from 1154 to 1166, succeeding his father Roger II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-i-of-the-netherlands"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/william-i-of-the-netherlands.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">William I of the Netherlands</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">William I was the first King of the Netherlands, reigning from 1815 to 1840.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-i-of-wurttemberg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/william-i-of-wurttemberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">William I of Württemberg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">William I was King of Württemberg from 1816 until his death in 1864.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-i-count-of-nassau-siegen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/william-i-count-of-nassau-siegen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">William I, Count of Nassau-Siegen</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">William I, Count of Nassau-Siegen, also called William the Rich, ruled the German lands of the house of Nassau from Dillenburg.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-i-duke-of-aquitaine"><img class="enc-thumb" src=