ip">William the Lion was King of Scots from 1165 to 1214, one of the longest reigns in Scottish history.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-the-silent"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/william-the-silent.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">William the Silent</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">William the Silent, Prince of Orange from 1544, was born at Dillenburg into the house of Nassau.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-the-victorious"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/william-the-victorious.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">William the Victorious</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">William the Victorious was Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg of the house of Welf.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-thornton"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/william-thornton.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">William Thornton</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">William Thornton was a physician, inventor and architect, born to a Quaker family on Jost Van Dyke in the British Virgin Islands.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-tolbert"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/william-tolbert.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">William Tolbert</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">William Tolbert was the 20th president of Liberia, serving from 1971, when he succeeded William Tubman, until 1980.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-tryon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/william-tryon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">William Tryon